# Scheduled jobs for this deployment's `cron` service (docker-compose.yml and
# docker-compose.production.yml). Busybox `crond` reads this file from `/etc/crontabs/root` — see
# docs/reference/ops.md#scheduled-jobs for what each job does and why it is safe to repeat.
#
# `db/run-script.ts` gives every entry point here a non-zero exit on failure and closes its Mongo
# connection on both paths, which is exactly the contract a scheduler wants.
#
# Every line below MUST name an existing `npm run` script, and every `reap:*`/`sweep:*` script in
# package.json MUST have a line below — tests/cross-cutting/scheduled-jobs.test.ts enforces both
# directions, since this file is a second place that has to agree with package.json and nothing
# else checks that it does.
#
# Staggered five minutes apart, nightly at low-traffic hours (the container's default TZ, UTC), so
# five jobs each opening their own Mongo connection do not all land on the pool at once.
#
# `sweep:webhook-retries` is the one job below NOT on that nightly schedule — it runs every
# minute, because OUTBOUND_WEBHOOKS.md's delayed-retry decision (c) makes the sweep interval the
# retry granularity: a webhook retry due in 5 seconds is only actually retried on the next minute
# boundary. A minute-scale query against an indexed `{ status, nextAttemptAt }` is cheap regardless
# of how the nightly jobs are staggered, so it needs no offset from them.
#
# Output redirects to /proc/1/fd/1 and /proc/1/fd/2 — PID 1's own stdout/stderr — rather than
# /dev/stdout: crond does not attach a cron job's stdout to the container's, so a plain redirect
# would go nowhere. /proc/1/fd/* reaches the container's real log stream regardless, which is what
# lets Promtail ship every run.
0  2 * * * cd /app && npm run reap:quarantine        >> /proc/1/fd/1 2>> /proc/1/fd/2
5  2 * * * cd /app && npm run reap:inactive-accounts >> /proc/1/fd/1 2>> /proc/1/fd/2
10 2 * * * cd /app && npm run reap:orders            >> /proc/1/fd/1 2>> /proc/1/fd/2
15 2 * * * cd /app && npm run reap:payments          >> /proc/1/fd/1 2>> /proc/1/fd/2
20 2 * * * cd /app && npm run sweep:order-effects    >> /proc/1/fd/1 2>> /proc/1/fd/2
*  * * * * cd /app && npm run sweep:webhook-retries  >> /proc/1/fd/1 2>> /proc/1/fd/2
